🛒 Superstore Sales Performance Analysis

Tracking Sales, Profitability & Business Growth | 2014–2017


📌 Project Overview

This project focuses on analyzing Superstore sales data from 2014 to 2017 to understand how the business performed across different customers, products, categories, segments, and geographic regions.

I built this Power BI dashboard to transform raw sales records into an interactive business performance report that makes it easier to identify revenue drivers, profitability patterns, customer activity, product performance, and sales trends over time.

Rather than looking at sales as individual transactions, I approached the analysis from a business perspective by exploring questions such as:

* How much revenue and profit did the business generate?
* Which states contribute the most to revenue?
* Which product categories drive sales?
* Which customer segments generate the most revenue?
* Which products contribute the most profit?
* How have sales changed over time?
* What areas of the business may require further attention?

The final dashboard brings these findings together in one interactive view, allowing users to explore business performance using Region and Customer ID filters.


🎯 Business Objective

The main objective of this project was to analyze sales performance and provide a clear view of the factors influencing revenue, profitability, customer activity, product performance, and business growth.

The analysis was designed to explore:

* Sales performance
* Profitability
* Customer activity
* Product contribution
* Regional performance
* Customer segmentation
* Sales trends

The goal was not simply to present numbers, but to make the data easier to understand and to be used for business decision-making.


